mestamps] from context (stale digests, schedule\n# anchors) instead of running date(1). Evidence (continuo 09-15): two\n# HISTORY.log lines claimed 2026-09-16 -- a day that had not happened --\n# and one line carried the literal unexpanded template [$(date -u ...)].\n# Evidence (aria): 13 FUTURE lines all-time, 7 of them +24h exactly\n# (c98, c136, session XI -- the model wrote the SCHEDULE's day with a\n# copied clock time). The commit that carries the line is the only\n# ground truth for when it was written.\n#\n# Refuses a staged HISTORY.log/USAGE.log change that ADDS a log line\n# (leading bracketed field) whose timestamp is more than FUTURE_TOL\n# ahead of NOW, or whose leading field is an unexpanded $(date) template.\n# The diff is scoped to the audit-log files ONLY -- prose in journals,\n# roadmaps, and docs that quotes or discusses templates is never scanned.\n# Within the audit logs, only the LEADING bracketed field is checked\n# (the timestamp slot); mid-text mentions are not flagged.\n\n[t+23:27/60:00 c71/300]"}]
